WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.690
All of show developer Peter Lenkov's reboots
of previous TV shows, including "MacGyver,"

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:12.300
"Magnum P.I.," and "Hawaii Five-0," share
the same fictional universe known as the "Lenkov-verse,"

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.790
and have been substantial hits for their parent
network CBS.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:20.599
However, the Lenkov-verse has seen a great
deal of controversy over the years.

00:00:20.599 --> 00:00:27.159
In 2017, regular "Hawaii Five-0" cast members
Daniel Dae Kim and Grace Park left the series

00:00:27.159 --> 00:00:33.240
over a salary dispute, given how they were
reportedly paid 10-15% less than series leads

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.790
Alex O'Loughlin and Scott Caan.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:41.470
Then in 2020, Lenkov was fired from the three
shows by CBS after multiple claims that he'd

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:47.220
fostered a toxic work environment, as well
as allegations that he was abusive and manipulative

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:48.310
on sets.

00:00:53.611 --> 00:01:00.481
"MacGyver" concluded in 2021 after five seasons,
and "Magnum" is still on the air as of 2022.

00:01:00.481 --> 00:01:04.561
Much of this, of course, is behind-the-scenes
stuff, and even really tense sets have been

00:01:04.561 --> 00:01:06.831
known to produce entertaining works.

00:01:06.831 --> 00:01:11.011
On the whole, "Hawaii Five-0" is precisely
the kind of action-packed police procedural

00:01:11.011 --> 00:01:14.481
drama that's an easy fit for a multiple-season
run.

00:01:14.481 --> 00:01:18.801
However, that doesn't mean the show is entirely
devoid of problematic moments in front of

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:19.801
the camera.

00:01:19.801 --> 00:01:23.951
In fact, all those off-screen problems might
have meant that nobody noticed how bleak and

00:01:23.951 --> 00:01:26.621
off-putting a particular Season 10 plot is.

00:01:26.621 --> 00:01:31.121
Let's take a look at the "Hawaii Five-O" scene
that the fans think went too far.

00:01:31.121 --> 00:01:36.430
In episode 14 of Season 10, Danny meets an
attractive woman at a bar, and they hit it

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:37.430
off.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:41.271
However, as they head home together, the pair
end up in a crash after Danny is forced to

00:01:41.271 --> 00:01:43.571
swerve to avoid an oncoming car.

00:01:43.571 --> 00:01:48.430
The woman is badly injured, and they're in
a remote area without cell reception.

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:53.591
Dramatic and sad scenes ensue, and in the
end, she passes away before help arrives without

00:01:53.591 --> 00:01:55.740
ever telling the devastated Danny her name.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:56.740
"What's so funny?"

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.331
"I got the luck like you said.

00:01:59.331 --> 00:02:02.860
I meet the girl of my dreams and we get in
a car accident."

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:07.061
The plot is definitely sad, but it arguably
feels off in a number of ways.

00:02:07.061 --> 00:02:11.491
Chief among them is the fact that the entire
thing seems to run against Danny's characterization

00:02:11.491 --> 00:02:15.842
— which is saying something, considering
that the show's had time to explore the character

00:02:15.842 --> 00:02:17.951
for years and years at this point.

00:02:17.951 --> 00:02:22.550
While Danny is incredibly faithful to his
friends, he's also a rather melancholic and

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:27.101
reserved figure who's incredibly unlikely
to open the creaky armor of his sarcastic

00:02:27.101 --> 00:02:29.221
exterior for a new acquaintance.

00:02:29.221 --> 00:02:34.250
As such, it seems out of character for Danny
to bond with someone so quickly — and unfair

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:38.841
to have the character go through another loss
after the murder of his partner and a messy

00:02:38.841 --> 00:02:39.841
divorce.

00:02:39.841 --> 00:02:43.431
This may be one of the reasons why some fans
feel the story is contrived.

00:02:43.431 --> 00:02:48.101
One "Hawaii Five-0" subreddit user pointed
out Danny's out-of-character behavior, and

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:53.020
felt that the storyline only happened as,
quote, "another go for Peter Lenkov to punish

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.020
the character."

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:57.641
As a whole, the episode is clearly not a fan-favorite
episode.

00:02:57.641 --> 00:03:03.781
In fact, with its comparatively meager 6.8
IMDb user rating, it's far and away the lowest-rated

00:03:03.781 --> 00:03:07.261
episode in the entire "Hawaii Five-0" Season
10.

00:03:07.261 --> 00:03:11.601
Apart from the way the episode both portrays
Danny in a strange way and puts him through

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:16.211
the emotional wringer by introducing a potential
love interest and taking her away within the

00:03:16.211 --> 00:03:21.050
span of a single episode's run time, viewers
have pointed out other issues in the episode,

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.380
as well.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:27.091
Multiple IMDb user reviews concurred that
Danny's behavior is off here, and not only

00:03:27.091 --> 00:03:29.050
in the dramatic death scene.

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:33.542
One User pointed out that his first aid skills
are completely wrong, and even said that he

00:03:33.542 --> 00:03:37.741
directly contributes to the woman's fate with
his clumsy attempts to save her.

00:03:37.741 --> 00:03:42.630
What's more, another user noted that the terrifying
incident is more or less forgotten after the

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:47.721
episode is over, since, quote, "the police
did not investigate or judge the driver and

00:03:47.721 --> 00:03:48.791
[they] never mention it again."

00:03:48.791 --> 00:03:53.451
"Come on, come on, come on.

00:03:53.451 --> 00:03:56.451
Come on!

00:03:56.451 --> 00:03:59.301
Somebody!."

00:03:59.301 --> 00:04:03.321
While Scott Caan gets a chance to flex his
dramatic muscles here, his character's big

00:04:03.321 --> 00:04:07.731
scene in this episode has clearly bothered
many people — as has a whole bunch of other

00:04:07.731 --> 00:04:09.171
stuff surrounding it.

00:04:09.171 --> 00:04:14.601
All in all, definitely not the finest hour
of "Hawaii Five-0."

